WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.236
And he turned to us and was like, come in on Monday and you're hired.
他转向我们说，周一来，你就被录用了。

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:10.191
And we walked out and we're so stunned that we got lost in the complex L shape floor plan of the.
我们走出去，惊呆了，迷失在复杂的 L 形平面图中。

00:00:10.191 --> 00:00:14.488
There's no way to get lost, but we all lost all the way down the hall.
没有办法迷路，但我们都迷路了。

00:00:14.488 --> 00:00:19.768
We turned the only corner, we turned the corner, the only corner of the whole hallway.
我们拐过唯一的拐角，我们拐过拐角，整个走廊唯一的拐角。

00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:23.759
And we turned the corner and like you can film this in your mind.
我们度过了难关，就像你可以在脑海中拍摄这一切一样。

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:24.987
It's it's high noon.
正是正午时分。

00:00:24.987 --> 00:00:36.406
And there are the other end is David Letterman, like standing alone, like I think he was like tossing a football, just standing there, like he's maybe going to kick our ass or something.
另一端是大卫·莱特曼（David Letterman），他就像一个人站着，我觉得他就像在扔一个足球，站在那里，好像他可能会踢我们的屁股什么的。

00:00:36.406 --> 00:00:39.659
And we say to him, do you know where the elevator is?
我们对他说，你知道电梯在哪里吗？

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.213
It's Josh, right?
是乔什，对吧？

00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:56.880
And we're welcome to a bonus episode of how we made your mother.
欢迎收看关于我们如何造就你母亲的额外剧集。

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:05.627
We heard the tale of how Craig and Carter came to write, how I met your mother.
我们听到了克雷格和卡特如何开始写作的故事，以及我如何遇见你母亲的故事。

00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:19.040
But there's an even deeper, richer backstory, how Craig met Carter and we're going to get into this twisty, windy mystery right now.
但还有一个更深刻、更丰富的背景故事，克雷格如何遇见卡特，我们现在将进入这个曲折、多风的谜团。

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:27.519
I want to get first the origin story of how you two met Carter and Craig or Craig and Carter.
我想先了解你们两个如何认识卡特和克雷格或克雷格和卡特的起源故事。

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:29.519
It's really Carter and Craig.
确实是卡特和克雷格。

00:01:29.519 --> 00:01:32.719
Tell us how you guys met and what were your first impressions of each other.
告诉我们你们是如何认识的以及你们对彼此的第一印象是什么。

00:01:32.719 --> 00:01:33.719
I'm just curious.
我只是好奇。

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:37.219
if you remember the moment you met each other?
你还记得你们相遇的那一刻吗？

00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:39.379
I don't remember, I don't remember this meeting.
我不记得了，我不记得这次会议。

00:01:39.379 --> 00:01:47.939
I, we were sort of both part of the, part of the furniture at Wesleyan for, for a good year and a half, I think before we actually like had a conversation.
我，我们都是卫斯理学院家具的一部分，整整一年半的时间，我想在我们真正喜欢进行一次对话之前。

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:49.140
I remember Craig played drums.
我记得克雷格打鼓。

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.540
That made him a very like, very in demand commodity in the, in the music world.
这使他成为音乐界非常受欢迎、非常抢手的商品。

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.379
I, I was like a singer and guitarist and not very good at either.
我，我就像一个歌手和吉他手，但两者都不太擅长。

00:01:56.379 --> 00:02:06.420
So like I wanted to be in a band really bad and no one was taking and Craig was in like seven bands, He had a prom set and he could play and he was really good.
所以就像我非常想加入一支乐队，但没有人接受，而克雷格参加了大约七个乐队，他有一个舞会演出，他可以演奏，而且他真的很棒。

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:10.900
And yeah, we sort of like English classes.
是的，我们有点喜欢英语课。

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:25.780
I think we were in some English store story writing classes and some like screenwriting classes and just sort of eyeballed each other from across the conference table.
我想我们参加了一些英语商店故事写作课程，还有一些类似的编剧课程，我们只是在会议桌对面互相注视着对方。

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.699
I'm going to create a hit TV show with that guy one day.
有一天我要和那个人一起制作一部热门电视节目。

00:02:28.699 --> 00:02:30.699
I just had a few.
我只吃了一些。

00:02:30.699 --> 00:02:33.580
Yeah, first of all, Carter's underselling his singing prowess.
是的，首先，卡特低估了他的歌唱实力。

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:40.259
He was an intimate, like once you actually got on there and sang everyone was like, wait a second, let's get that, like then you would then the table's turned.
他是一个亲密的人，就像一旦你真正登上那里并唱歌，每个人都会说，等一下，让我们开始吧，就像然后你就会扭转局面一样。

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:41.740
No one gave a shit about the drummer anymore.
没有人再关心鼓手了。

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.139
So I just want to make that very clear.
所以我只想说得非常清楚。

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:45.379
I tried.
我试过。

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:49.060
I, someone heard me hollering in the showers and that was it.
我，有人听到我在淋浴时大喊大叫，就是这样。

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:16.789
Was there a moment when you guys made each other laugh for you, you, you started thinking comedically?
有没有那么一瞬间，你们让彼此为你而笑，你，你开始用喜剧的方式思考？

00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:18.909
I remember we were in a screenwriting class together.
我记得我们一起上编剧课。

00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:24.036
I feel like before we were really friends, what really made us friends is playing in a band together.
我觉得在我们成为真正的朋友之前，真正让我们成为朋友的是一起在乐队里演奏。

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:26.827
We finally got in a band together a junior year, right?
我们终于在大三的时候组建了一个乐队，对吧？

00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:33.069
Carter and then we're in bands together the whole second half of college and to this day, we still play in a band together.
卡特和我们整个大学后半段都在乐队里，直到今天，我们仍然一起在乐队里演奏。

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:41.362
That was very much our first way we worked together was playing in a band but we weren't like close because Carter was the lead singer.
我们合作的第一个方式就是在乐队中演奏，但我们的关系并不亲密，因为卡特是主唱。

00:03:41.362 --> 00:03:46.460
We were in a nine piece soul band with like four horns and I was behind a drum set.
我们在一个九人灵魂乐队中，有四个号角，我在鼓组后面。

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.978
In the band we barely had a conversation.
在乐队里我们几乎没有交谈。

00:03:48.978 --> 00:03:50.146
It was really true.
这确实是真的。

00:03:50.146 --> 00:03:53.770
Like seven is like, I feel like that's that's conservative.
就像七一样，我觉得那是保守的。

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.858
I think we got upwards of like 12.
我想我们大概有 12 个以上。

00:03:55.858 --> 00:03:59.052
It was like the size of like a, like an early 2000s.
它的大小就像 2000 年代初期一样。

00:03:59.052 --> 00:04:00.342
The polyphonic spree.
复调狂欢。

00:04:00.342 --> 00:04:01.939
It was a full, full choir.
这是一个完整的合唱团。

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:07.529
Yeah, I think we had like two rows of risers, but you know, it was, it was a lot of people.
是的，我想我们有两排立管，但你知道，有很多人。

00:04:07.529 --> 00:04:12.811
So we didn't really, yeah, we didn't, it was like the real moment I feel like was MTV.
所以我们真的没有，是的，我们没有，这就像我觉得 MTV 的真实时刻。

00:04:12.811 --> 00:04:17.909
We, we, Craig and I got a, that we played in this band together all June your year.
我们，我们，克雷格和我，我们整个六月都在这个乐队里一起演奏。

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:29.790
And then I feel like the way I retell this story, and maybe this is true, or maybe this is apocryphal, but I feel like maybe we didn't know each, didn't know that the other was applying to this internship, but then we showed up in New York City.
然后我觉得我重述这个故事的方式，也许这是真的，或者也许这是杜撰的，但我觉得也许我们并不认识，不知道对方正在申请这份实习，但后来我们出现在纽约市。

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:45.870
Like we went in for like on a weekday, and in some time in the spring of, I guess it would be 1996, to both to interview for an internship at MTV to in their development department, which we didn't, I don't think we even knew what development meant.
就像我们在一个工作日，在春天的某个时候，我想那是 1996 年，两人都去 MTV 面试他们的开发部门的实习机会，但我们没有，我想我们甚至不知道开发意味着什么。

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:51.110
I thought, like, are we, like, hanging photographs on paper or on the screen?
我想，我们是把照片挂在纸上还是屏幕上？

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.509
Plus, there's never going to be an era where MTV does anything but play music videos.
另外，永远不会有一个 MTV 除了播放音乐视频之外什么都不做的时代。

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:57.149
So what kind of shows are they going to play?
那么他们会表演什么样的节目呢？

00:04:57.149 --> 00:05:00.189
So wait, so this was between your junior and senior year?
那么等等，这是你大三和大四之间的事情吗？

00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:01.189
That's it.
就是这样。

00:05:01.189 --> 00:05:02.189
Yes.
是的。

00:05:02.189 --> 00:05:09.670
So then, I know that you guys, by the time you graduated, is it true you had, like, a comedy packet together, just the two of you?
那么，我知道你们，当你们毕业的时候，你们真的有一个喜剧包吗？只有你们两个人在一起吗？

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:10.670
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.670
Yeah.
是的。

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.670
We started writing it.
我们开始写它。

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.310
that summer working at MTV.
那年夏天在 MTV 工作。

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:21.670
And again, that was after a year of being in a band at some point during which Carter was like, I think there's a drummer back there behind some of those horn players.
再说一次，那是在乐队呆了一年之后的某个时候，卡特就像是，我认为在一些喇叭手后面有一个鼓手。

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.670
And I was like, I said, I'm like, I'm not sure.
我说，我想，我不确定。

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.189
He looks like the guy that sings the songs.
他看起来就像那个唱歌的人。

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:29.589
We were just like, we weren't close in the band because the band was 45 people.
我们当时就想，我们在乐队中的关系并不亲密，因为乐队有 45 人。

00:05:29.589 --> 00:05:41.029
But we then, we really bonded at MTV, but we'd also already had a screenwriting class and I'll embarrass Carter again by saying, first of all, he was a great singer and he was very in demand to be a singer.
但后来我们在 MTV 上真正建立了联系，但我们也已经上了编剧课，我会再次让卡特感到尴尬，首先，他是一位伟大的歌手，而且非常需要他成为一名歌手。

00:05:41.029 --> 00:05:43.870
And second, he was in a screenwriting class with me.
其次，他和我一起上编剧课。

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.750
And he was the best fucking writer.
他是最棒的作家。

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.310
He was, well, I wanted you.
他是，好吧，我想要你。

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:54.189
I wanted you, but you Carter was like his writing so stood out in the screenwriting class.
我想要你，但你卡特就像他的作品一样在编剧班上脱颖而出。

00:05:54.189 --> 00:05:55.509
It was just like a dinky little, right?
它就像一个很小的小东西，对吧？

00:05:55.509 --> 00:06:03.910
Like 10 or 12 people, we sort of volunteered scenes and you were like the only person cobbling together, using it to cobble together a feature length script.
就像 10 或 12 个人一样，我们有点自愿制作场景，而你就像是唯一一个拼凑在一起的人，用它拼凑出一个长篇剧本。

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.350
And I just remember going like the balls on this fucking guy.
我只记得我对这个该死的家伙很感兴趣。

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:07.189
Oh, right.
哦，对了。

00:06:07.189 --> 00:06:09.350
But with admiration, I was like, this guy, right?
但带着钦佩之情，我想，这家伙，对吗？

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:12.829
You were putting, I remember when the script was, I remember it was good.
你在写，我记得剧本当时写的，我记得那很好。

00:06:12.829 --> 00:06:15.310
It was insane and funny and violent.
这是疯狂、有趣和暴力的。

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:18.269
It was like, it was like, it was like, it was like, it was like, it was like, it was like, it was like, Heather is ish.
就像，就像，就像，就像，就像，就像，就像，希瑟是这样。

00:06:18.269 --> 00:06:28.029
I feel like you told me that there was a lot of buzz about Carter before he even got to school because he had a play being produced off Broadway and he was late for school.
我感觉你告诉我卡特在上学之前就已经有很多关于他的传闻了，因为他在百老汇正在制作一部戏剧，而他上学迟到了。

00:06:28.029 --> 00:06:29.029
Is that right?
是这样吗？

00:06:29.029 --> 00:06:30.029
That is true.
确实如此。

00:06:30.029 --> 00:06:31.029
Yes.
是的。

00:06:31.029 --> 00:06:32.029
I had a play that I wrote.
我有一个自己写的剧本。

00:06:32.029 --> 00:06:47.529
I was really into playwriting in high school, just fell in love with theater and I wrote a few short plays and on a whim, just sent one of them into the New York Young Playwrights Festival, which was like a big contest.
我在高中时非常喜欢剧本创作，只是爱上了戏剧，我写了一些短剧，一时兴起，就把其中的一部送到了纽约青年剧作家节，这就像一场大型比赛。

00:06:47.529 --> 00:07:00.370
At the time, it was a, it was a, it was a, I mean, this is before YouTube, it was back when like, there was no like, you know, you had to like physically print something out and send it out to New York for any chance of anyone ever seeing it, you know.
当时，这是，这是，这是，我的意思是，这是在 YouTube 之前，当时还没有类似的东西，你知道，你必须打印一些东西并将其发送到纽约，以便任何人有机会看到它，你知道。

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:18.225
So it was, I just sent this thing in and it ended up winning and the prize was a two months production of my show as part of a night of one acts at young playwrights horizons theater in New York, which I later found out, like, oh, that's actually a really good theater.
事情就是这样，我刚刚把这个东西寄了进去，它最终获胜了，奖品是我的节目为期两个月的制作，作为纽约年轻剧作家地平线剧院的一个表演之夜的一部分，我后来发现，哦，那实际上是一个非常好的剧院。

00:07:18.225 --> 00:07:20.349
It's kind of, it was a big deal.
有点，这是一件大事。

00:07:20.349 --> 00:07:23.734
And it was, the play was directed by Michael Mayer.
确实，该剧由迈克尔·梅尔执导。

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:24.234
Yeah.
是的。

00:07:24.234 --> 00:07:29.876
I always find this amazing at what age did you say I want to, I want to write things.
我总是觉得这很神奇，你说我想在什么年纪，我想写东西。

00:07:29.876 --> 00:07:31.337
I want to write plays.
我想写戏剧。

00:07:31.337 --> 00:07:32.863
I want to write movies.
我想写电影。

00:07:32.863 --> 00:07:36.182
I think it was like, I, I'm going to say I was 14.
我想这就像，我，我会说我14岁。

00:07:36.182 --> 00:07:59.414
I was really into, into watching stuff, like I just was a voracious consumer of television and movies and you know it was the golden age of video stores and so I had a bunch of friends who were really into like zombie movies and stuff and like I, but then it was actually, I took a trip to the library, the public library which my first time got out.
我真的很喜欢看东西，就像我是电视和电影的贪婪消费者一样，你知道这是音像店的黄金时代，所以我有一群朋友非常喜欢僵尸电影和东西，就像我一样，但事实上，我去了图书馆，我第一次出去的公共图书馆。

00:07:59.414 --> 00:08:07.048
I found there was a book called How to Write a a movie in 21 days by, I think it was Vicki King was maybe the name.
我发现有一本书叫《如何在 21 天里写一部电影》，我想这可能是 Vicki King 的名字。

00:08:06.879 --> 00:08:10.079
I can't remember the person who wrote it, but it's the book that changed my life.
我不记得是谁写的，但这本书改变了我的生活。

00:08:10.079 --> 00:08:20.279
I was like a little slim, a little volume stuck between their film section of the Shaker Heights public library, but I was like, oh, write a film.
我就像一个瘦小的小卷，卡在谢克高地公共图书馆的电影区之间，但我想，哦，写一部电影。

00:08:20.279 --> 00:08:21.279
You can do that.
你可以这么做。

00:08:21.279 --> 00:08:23.240
I guess films get written.
我猜电影是写出来的。

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:28.199
Someone has to write down on paper what the actors are going to say, and that just kicked the door down.
必须有人把演员要说的话写在纸上，这就把门踢开了。

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:29.920
And after that, I'm going to write screenplays.
之后，我会写剧本。

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:36.172
Do you ever find it astonishing, like, I always think a 15 year old teenager decided what I was going to do for my life?
你有没有觉得很惊讶，比如，我总是认为一个 15 岁的青少年决定了我一生要做什么？

00:08:36.172 --> 00:08:40.914
Just like how astonishing that is, like a 14 year old boy said you're going to be a writer.
就像一个 14 岁的男孩说你要成为一名作家一样，这是多么令人惊讶。

00:08:40.914 --> 00:08:43.884
I feel like, do you know the show Passing Strange by Stu?
我觉得，你知道 Stu 的《Passing Strange》吗？

00:08:43.884 --> 00:08:44.457
Yeah, yeah.
是啊是啊。

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:45.707
He has a line like that.
他有这样的台词。

00:08:45.707 --> 00:08:47.166
It's kind of the same thing.
这是一样的事情。

00:08:47.166 --> 00:08:57.014
Yeah, it's like this ding dong, who doesn't know anything about anything is, but having some sort of like the life visionary, almost prophetic sense of like, this this would be a good idea.
是的，就像这个叮咚，什么都不知道，但是有某种像生活的远见，几乎是预言般的感觉，这将是一个好主意。

00:08:57.014 --> 00:08:58.838
We should do this impossible thing.
我们应该做这件不可能的事。

00:08:58.838 --> 00:08:59.338
Yeah.
是的。

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.839
And it was absolutely right in all of our cases.
在我们所有的案例中，这都是绝对正确的。

00:09:01.839 --> 00:09:04.027
That is what we were supposed to be doing.
这就是我们应该做的。

00:09:04.027 --> 00:09:11.166
You know, it's funny about reminiscing about college because Alec Lavar, producer extraordinaire went to Wesleyan with us, me and Carter.
你知道，回忆大学时光很有趣，因为出色的制片人亚历克·拉瓦尔 (Alec Lavar) 和我们、我和卡特一起去了卫斯理学院。

00:09:11.166 --> 00:09:17.106
And I often feel like Josh went to Wesleyan because he played a guy who went to Wesleyan on how I met your mother.
我经常觉得乔什去了卫斯理安，因为他在我如何认识你母亲的过程中扮演了一个去了卫斯理安的人。

00:09:17.106 --> 00:09:18.773
I mean, forget that you did Rex.
我的意思是，忘记你做了雷克斯。

00:09:18.773 --> 00:09:19.815
We still don't know.
我们仍然不知道。

00:09:19.815 --> 00:09:21.952
He, yeah, he was just disguised as Dr. X.
他，是的，他只是伪装成X博士。

